   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The verb ir",
     "texto": [
      "The verb **ir** (to go) is irregular. It is conjugated like this:\n\n- yo **voy** (I go)\n- tú **vas** (you go)\n- él / ella / usted **va** (he / she / you formal go)\n- nosotros **vamos** (we go)\n- vosotros **vais** (you all go)\n- ellos **van** (they go)\n\nTo say where you are going, use **a**:\n\n- Voy **a** la playa. (I go to the beach.)\n- Voy **al** centro. (I go to the centre.)\n\nNotice: **a + el = al**. And in the plural, **a + los = a los**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Al, del and how to get around",
     "texto": [
      "Two contractions you need to master:\n\n- **a + el = al**: «Voy **al** centro».\n- **de + el = del**: «Vengo **del** trabajo».\n\nYou never say «a el» or «de el».\n\nAnd for getting around:\n\n- **en metro** (by metro), **en autobús** (by bus), **en tren** (by train), **en coche** (by car), **en bici** (by bike)\n- **a pie** (on foot), when you are walking"
     ],
